Based on the IE11 screenshot (every date stacked in a single column, missing proper flex layout, and the bad keyframes rule), IE11 is choking on two things:

1. The “animation” shorthand is malformed (missing the colon), so IE11 never animates/translates the weeks in or out.  
2. IE11 does not understand the non‐standard “flex-justify: between;” shorthand, so each week collapses to a single column (only the first day of the week is visible).

Here are two simple *SEARCH/REPLACE* patches in src/js/components/Calendar/StyledCalendar.js to fix both:

